# SABOTAGE: T74 (spec §I1 CRM two-way email sync) gate sabotage — defeats the MAILBOX seam's
# FAIL-HONEST adapter contract (ADR-014/024/026). `Samen.Mailbox.FakeProvider.guarded/4` is the
# single chokepoint every network-touching callback (connect/disconnect/fetch/send/parse_push)
# routes through: with no credentials it returns `{:error, :not_configured}` and does NOTHING.
# This patch drops the `configured?/1` check and runs the ok-branch unconditionally — the exact
# canned-`{:ok, _}`-for-work-it-did-not-do lie the contract abolishes. An unconfigured mailbox
# would then report a successful connect, a successful (empty) fetch, and a fake send receipt,
# so "no provider wired" and "connected, nothing new" become indistinguishable. The CONFIGURED
# positive controls stay green (they were already taking the ok-branch), so the flip is
# non-vacuous. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/mailbox_provider_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: EVERY network-touching callback returns {:error, :not_configured}
# MUST_FAIL: it records NO calls and returns NO fake data when unconfigured
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/mailbox/fake_provider.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/mailbox/fake_provider.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/mailbox/fake_provider.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/mailbox/fake_provider.ex
@@ -157,13 +157,9 @@
   # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   # Private
 
-  defp guarded(callback, args, config, ok_fun) do
-    if configured?(config) do
-      record_call(callback, args)
-      ok_fun.()
-    else
-      {:error, :not_configured}
-    end
+  defp guarded(callback, args, _config, ok_fun) do
+    record_call(callback, args)
+    ok_fun.()
   end
 
   defp record_call(callback, args),
